[38;2;124;124;124mcorresponds to an element of π_4(BSU(2)) = Z, which is the second Chern class. [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mSo \bar{h} is the map classified by c_2 = k. This makes sense: the second Chern [0m[38;2;124;124;124mclass of P is k, and this is captured by the degree of \bar{h} on the top cell.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet me write up the proof.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mActually, let me double-check the cofibration sequence argument. We have A = [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mX^{(3)} (the 3-skeleton), X the full space, and X/A ≅ S^4 (since X has a single [0m[38;2;124;124;124mtop cell e^4, collapsing the 3-skeleton gives S^4). The cofibration sequence is [0m[38;2;124;124;124mA → X → X/A → ΣA → ...[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mFor any space Y, this gives an exact sequence of pointed sets:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m... → [ΣA, Y] → [X/A, Y] → [X, Y] → [A, Y][0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThe map [X, Y] → [A, Y] is restriction. The image of [X/A, Y] → [X, Y] is the [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mset of homotopy classes of maps X → Y whose restriction to A is null-homotopic.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo [g^*: [S^4, BSU(2)] → [X, BSU(2)]] has image = {maps h: X → BSU(2) : h|_A [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mnull-homotopic}.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSince [A, BSU(2)] = * (because A is 3-dim and BSU(2) is 3-connected), every h [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mhas h|_A null-homotopic. So every h is in the image, i.e., every h factors [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mthrough g.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThis is clean. The answer is yes.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet me also verify: is BSU(2) really 3-connected? SU(2) ≅ S^3. π_0(SU(2)) = 0 [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m(connected), π_1(SU(2)) = 0, π_2(SU(2)) = 0, π_3(SU(2)) = Z. For BG, π_n(BG) = [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mπ_{n-1}(G). So:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- π_1(BSU(2)) = π_0(SU(2)) = 0[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- π_2(BSU(2)) = π_1(SU(2)) = 0[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- π_3(BSU(2)) = π_2(SU(2)) = 0[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- π_4(BSU(2)) = π_3(SU(2)) = Z[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mYes, BSU(2) is 3-connected. Good.[0m

